title: $:/plugins/rimir/knowledge-app/doc/architecture
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

<$transclude $tiddler="$:/plugins/rimir/doc-template/templates/page">
<$fill $name="body">

!! Layers

# ''Storage'' — plain TW tiddlers under `knowledge/…`, tagged `$:/tags/rimir/knowledge-app/note`, with `kn.tier` field.
# ''Resolution'' — namespace plugin handles `[[Foo]]` resolution via its 9-stage pipeline (literal → alias → mount → pseudo → walk-up → unresolved). The app enables walk-up + aliases + pseudo-expansion on install.
# ''App shell'' — appify framework. App declared at `$:/plugins/rimir/knowledge-app/apps/knowledge` with channels `section topic note` and a `topbar-sidebar-main` layout.
# ''Views'' — five sections: Home, Browse, Note, Write, Search. Switched via `section` channel; clicking a topic in the sidebar navigates with `topic` set.

!! Channels

| Channel | Set by | Read by |
|`section`| Topbar buttons, breadcrumb, `$action-statewrap-navigate` | Splits config (decides which view to render) |
|`topic` | Sidebar topic-tree buttons | Browse view (filters by topic prefix) |
|`note` | Note-card buttons, search results, capture | Note view (chooses which note to render) |

!! Filter helpers

`filters/helpers.tid` exposes:

* `\function knowledge.notes()` — all notes via the system tag
* `\function knowledge.orphans()` — notes with zero `ns-backlinks`
* `\function knowledge.dead-ends()` — notes with zero `ns-forwardlinks`
* `\function knowledge.stubs()` — notes whose body is shorter than the configured threshold
* `\function knowledge.broken()` — notes whose body contains an unresolved `[[ref]]`

The broken-ref detector is a JS filter operator (`knowledge-has-broken-ref`) that scans the body and asks the resolver about each `[[…]]` match.

!! Custom pseudo

`pseudo/_index.js` (module-type `rimir-ns-pseudo`) — `_index` segment resolves to `index` or `README` if either exists under the preceding prefix. Use inside an absolute ref like `[[knowledge/topics/foo/_index]]`.

!! Type-specific forms

Each note type (defined in `config/types.tid`) can opt into two extension points:

# ''Capture form'' — `forms/capture-<type>`. Transcluded inside the quick-capture modal between the type select and the body textarea (only when the chosen type has a matching tiddler). Inputs bind to dedicated state tiddlers under `$:/state/rimir/knowledge-app/capture/<type>/<field>` so they survive type-switching and don't collide with the generic title/body state. The Create action of the modal applies the captured values via a per-type `<$action-setfield>` block, then resets that state.
# ''Render form'' — `forms/render-<type>`. Transcluded in `views/note` ''above'' the body, with the outer `<<noteTitle>>` variable in scope. Reads `kn.*` fields from the note and produces a structured card (table, embeds, controls). Free to provide its own inline-edit affordances (the `source` form uses one state tiddler per note at `$:/state/rimir/knowledge-app/source-edit/<noteTitle>` whose text is the field name being edited).

Helpers shared between the two halves of a type live in `forms/<type>-helpers.tid` and are pulled in via `\import`. The `source` type uses `forms/source-helpers.tid` for `knowledge.yt-id`, `knowledge.medium-icon`, `knowledge.consume-icon`.

Adding a new type is therefore: declare it in `config/types.tid` and (optionally) add `forms/capture-<id>.tid` and/or `forms/render-<id>.tid`. No core code change.

</$fill>
</$transclude>
